# rollguard-site — everything committed here is served publicly at rollguard.app.
#
# This file is not about keeping the tree tidy. It is about keeping working files
# off a public URL. Added 2026-09-12, after devpost-gallery/ (17 working images,
# including an uncropped founder photo) and Apple's marketing-tools zip sat
# untracked in this tree on a day `git add -A` was being run here.
#
# NOTE ON SCOPE: .gitignore governs `git add` on this machine. It does NOT
# govern uploads made through the GitHub web UI (Add file -> Upload files),
# which is the other way images reach this repo. That path stays a human check.

# --- Devpost / marketing working sets ---------------------------------------
devpost-gallery/
*-3x2.*

# --- Archives ---------------------------------------------------------------
# A zip is invisible to every text-level check this project runs: the A7 floor
# sweep recorded "full-site grep: zero 'iOS 17' remains" — true of every text
# file and false of the repo, because panels-v4.zip served a stale "iOS 17+"
# closer from the live press page for eleven days.
# The press kit's own zips are published deliberately — excepted below.
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.tar
*.gz
*.tgz
!press-kit/*.zip

# --- Camera originals and raw/working image formats -------------------------
# Published photos are committed EXIF-stripped (images/README.md). These
# formats are never published and carry full capture metadata by default —
# about-on-the-water.jpg arrived 2026-09-01 with GPS embedded.
# .jpg/.png are deliberately NOT ignored: they are the published formats.
*.heic
*.HEIC
*.heif
*.HEIF
*.dng
*.DNG
*.cr2
*.CR2
*.nef
*.NEF
*.arw
*.ARW
*.tif
*.TIF
*.tiff
*.TIFF
*.psd
*.PSD
*.ai
*.sketch
*.fig
*.xcf

# --- Screen recordings and working video ------------------------------------
# Published video is .mp4 (press-kit/rollguard-preview*.mp4). Screen recordings
# come off the iPhone as .mov and are capture working files.
*.mov
*.MOV
*.m4v
*.M4V
*.avi

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# There is no server and no build step, so nothing here should ever need one.
# A file that did would be served as plain text at a public URL.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
*.keystore
secrets.*

# --- OS and editor cruft ----------------------------------------------------
# .DS_Store is not merely noise: it lists directory contents, including files
# since deleted, and would be readable at rollguard.app/.DS_Store.
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# --- Scratch, drafts, backups -----------------------------------------------
scratch/
tmp/
temp/
drafts/
*-draft.*
*-wip.*
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*.log

# --- Tooling (none today; guard in case any is added) -----------------------
node_modules/
.cache/

# --- Outreach, correspondence and working documents -------------------------
# PRESS_OUTREACH_EMAILS.txt — 43 KB naming sixteen journalists and the angle
# used on each — sat untracked in this root on 2026-09-13. NOTHING HERE CAUGHT
# IT: the first pass covered images, archives and secrets, and a .txt at the
# repo root is SERVED, so `git add -A` would have published the entire press
# strategy at rollguard.app/PRESS_OUTREACH_EMAILS.txt.
# robots.txt is excepted — the one .txt a static site legitimately serves.
*.txt
!robots.txt
*.eml
*.msg
*.docx
*.doc
*.rtf
*.pages
*.odt
# Name-based, so a future PRESS_OUTREACH.md or pitch-list.html is caught too —
# the hazard is the CONTENT, and it does not always arrive as a .txt.
*outreach*
*OUTREACH*
*pitch*
*PITCH*
